# Cursor agent operating rules — Marketing Knowledge Garden

You are working inside the Marketing Knowledge Garden (MKG), one vertical
of The Knowledge Gardens ecosystem. The Architect is the orchestrator;
you are a sub-agent unless explicitly told otherwise.

## Read these first, every time
1. `MKG_PROJECT_STATE.md` — what cycle we're in, what's blocked, what shipped.
2. `MKG_LESSONS.md` — every rule we've ever learned. Many are PROVISIONAL.
3. The brief in `dispatch/cycle-NNN-job-N-*.md` you're assigned to.

## Brand rules (auto-reject if violated)
- Background: parchment `#f5f0e8`. Never dark.
- Display type: Cormorant Garamond italic. Tech labels: Space Mono uppercase.
- Palette: Teal `#1A5C5C`, Copper `#B87333`, Steel `#71797E`, Cream `#FBF8F3`,
  Ink `#2C2C2C`. Per-entity accent color override allowed.
- Aesthetic: Victorian botanical herbarium meets engineering schematic.
- UI: tabs (Profile / Architecture / Intelligence / Compare). Never scroll-
  cinematic.
- Compass + Conveyor Belt motifs required on every Species Experience surface.
- Every entity page emits valid JSON-LD.
- Next.js: `output: "export"` is sacred. Never remove.

## Code rules
- TypeScript everywhere. No `any` without an explicit comment.
- Server-only secrets via Supabase service role key. Never ship to client.
- Reading data: Supabase client when API exists; embedded JSON only allowed
  before the API ships.
- Components: function components, named exports, one default per file.
- Style: Tailwind + the design tokens in `src/styles/tokens.css`. No inline
  hex values for brand colors.

## Research rules
- Every claim → at least one row in `citations`.
- Funding figures require a primary news/PR/Crunchbase citation. Vendor
  marketing pages don't count for funding.
- Unknown = `null`. Never invent.
- Confidence: high (clear primary source), medium (one plausible source),
  low (mention only — flag for re-verification).

## Workflow rules
- One brief = one job = one branch. Branch name: `agent/<role>/<job-id>`.
- Mark dispatch state in `dispatch_log` (or in the brief's frontmatter) when
  starting and when handing back.
- Verify your own work before handback: brand audit (UI), citation audit
  (research), JSON-LD validation (entity emitters), schema-parses (SQL).
- Architect rejects undocumented work. Write what you did, what you didn't,
  and what you escalated.

## What to escalate
- Brand-rule violations you can't fix on your own.
- Funding/legal claims you can't verify.
- Schema needs that the current shape can't accommodate.
- Anything that requires a new env var or external service auth.
